"""
Instagram Maximum-Data Collector
================================
Project 3 of the Content Intelligence System.

Purpose
-------
Collect as much reliable, accessible historical/current Instagram public-account
and post metadata as possible into instagram.db.

Source strategy
---------------
1. Instaloader is the primary public-profile/post collector. Current Instaloader
   provides Profile.from_username(), resumable profile post iteration, post
   metadata, comments, and session loading. No media files are downloaded.
2. Optional authenticated Instaloader session improves access where Instagram
   requires login. Supply INSTAGRAM_LOGIN_USERNAME and optionally
   INSTAGRAM_SESSION_FILE. Do not put passwords in this script.
3. yt-dlp is an optional per-post enrichment source. It is not treated as the
   authoritative discovery source because Instagram's web surface is volatile.
4. Optional Meta Graph API support can be added later for owned/eligible
   professional-account insights; this collector deliberately does not depend on
   that API for arbitrary public accounts.

Design goals
------------
- GUI with Start / Stop / Export / DB-folder controls.
- Real worker-process boundary so Stop can terminate a slow collector.
- Immediate durable persistence for every discovered post.
- Historical snapshots and post ingestion state.
- Idempotent/deduplicated comments and sidecar items.
- Raw Instaloader node capture plus optional raw yt-dlp metadata.
- Incremental recent-post window plus full-catalog mode.
- Rate-limit/challenge detection with persisted cooldown and pending post/account.
- Never download media files.

Installation
------------
pip install -U -r instagram_requirements.txt

Optional login session
----------------------
Set:
  INSTAGRAM_LOGIN_USERNAME=your_instagram_login
  INSTAGRAM_SESSION_FILE=/path/to/session-your_instagram_login

An Instaloader session file can be created with Instaloader's normal login flow.
The collector will load it when present. Public/anonymous collection is attempted
when no session is configured.
"""


