-------
Collect as much reliable, accessible historical/current TikTok account and video
metadata as possible into a dedicated SQLite database: tiktok.db.

Design goals
------------
1. Accept TikTok @handles, profile URLs, and video URLs.
2. Use yt-dlp's maintained TikTok extractor for public profile/video discovery and
   rich public video metadata.
3. Preserve raw TikTok HTML/JSON and sanitized yt-dlp metadata in SQLite.
4. Keep historical snapshots for accounts and videos.
5. Maintain incremental discovery / resume state so interrupted runs do not lose
   already-committed data.
6. Make every discovered video visible in the GUI and persist it immediately.
7. Keep a real process boundary so Stop can terminate the collector even during a
   slow network call.
8. Detect TikTok HTTP 429/rate-limit responses and persist a cooldown/pending item.
9. Optionally use the official TikTok Research API when an approved access token is
   supplied for richer public account/video/comment data.
10. Never download media files; only metadata/caption payloads/technical formats.

Notes
-----
TikTok's web surface changes frequently. yt-dlp currently has an actively maintained
TikTok extractor, but its issue tracker also contains recent TikTok breakages. The
collector therefore records raw responses and errors rather than assuming every
profile will always resolve. If a profile cannot be enumerated by yt-dlp, the run
keeps whatever public page data was successfully captured.

Optional files
--------------
- tiktok_cookies.json : browser-exported cookies for TikTok. Not required for public
  pages. Keep account cookies out of source control.

Optional environment variable
------------------------------
TIKTOK_RESEARCH_ACCESS_TOKEN
    Approved TikTok Research Tools client access token. This is NOT required for the
    normal public web/yt-dlp collector. If absent, Research API collection is disabled.

Dependencies
------------
pip install -U requests "yt-dlp[default]"
